<section class="legal-page container"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR LEARNING SPACE, RESPECTED</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="legal-intro">This policy describes the data handled by this BrainLoop installation. BrainLoop is an independent student software engineering project.</p><article class="legal-copy"><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>When you register, BrainLoop stores your full name, email address, and a password hash. It also stores the decks and flashcards you create, card schedules, and your review history. Your password is not stored in plain text.</p><h2>How your information is used</h2><p>Your information enables account access, private study materials, scheduled reviews, search, and study analytics. Review timestamps and study-day calculations use UTC. BrainLoop does not include advertising, third-party analytics, or external authentication services.</p><h2>Cookies and security records</h2><p>A necessary session cookie keeps you signed in and protects forms. It is HttpOnly and SameSite protected, and uses Secure when this installation is configured for HTTPS. Sign-in abuse controls may retain limited attempt information. Technical error logs may be written by the hosting environment.</p><h2>Access and control</h2><p>Your application data is accessible through your account. You can update your name, email, and password in Settings, remove your own cards and decks, and export your decks as CSV. The operator of a hosted installation controls its server, backups, access logs, retention, and any requests requiring direct database administration.</p><h2>Data storage</h2><p>Application data is stored in a MySQL/MariaDB database managed by the hosting operator and accessed through PHP PDO. The hosting operator is responsible for server access, encrypted transport, backups, and deployment security. Deleting a deck removes its cards, scheduling data, and associated review records from the active database; backup copies are managed separately by the operator.</p><h2>Sharing and external services</h2><p>This codebase does not send your learning data to an external API. Hosting providers may process server data under their own terms. Do not add sensitive personal, medical, financial, or confidential information to flashcards unless you understand the protections of the installation you use.</p><h2>Questions and changes</h2><p>For questions about a particular hosted installation, contact its operator using the contact information they provide. The project team is listed on the <a href="<?= e(url('/about')) ?>">About BrainLoop</a> page. A hosting operator should adapt this policy to their actual deployment and applicable requirements before offering a public service.</p></article></section>
